# WhatsApp Chatbot - News Fetch Cron Job
#
# This cron job fetches news articles every 6 hours (at 0:00, 6:00, 12:00, 18:00)
# The news fetching runs inside the Docker container, triggered from the host crontab.
#
# Installation (on host machine):
#   1. Copy this file to /etc/cron.d/whatsapp-news-fetch
#   2. Ensure the user has proper Docker permissions
#   3. Or add to user crontab: crontab -e
#
# Requirements:
#   - Docker must be installed and running
#   - The whatsapp-chatbot container must be running
#   - The user running cron must have docker permissions (or use sudo)

SHELL=/bin/bash
PATH=/usr/local/sbin:/usr/local/bin:/sbin:/bin:/usr/sbin:/usr/bin

# Run every 6 hours at minute 0
# Uses docker exec to run the news CLI inside the container
# Adjust CONTAINER_NAME if your container has a different name
0 */6 * * * docker exec whatsapp-chatbot node dist/commands/news-cli.js 100 >> /var/log/whatsapp-news-fetch.log 2>&1

# Alternative: Run at specific times (6am, 12pm, 6pm, 12am)
# 0 0,6,12,18 * * * docker exec whatsapp-chatbot node dist/commands/news-cli.js 100 >> /var/log/whatsapp-news-fetch.log 2>&1

# If your cron user doesn't have Docker permissions, use sudo:
# 0 */6 * * * sudo docker exec whatsapp-chatbot node dist/commands/news-cli.js 100 >> /var/log/whatsapp-news-fetch.log 2>&1

# Create log directory if it doesn't exist (run once manually)
# sudo mkdir -p /var/log && sudo touch /var/log/whatsapp-news-fetch.log && sudo chmod 666 /var/log/whatsapp-news-fetch.log

# To test manually: docker exec whatsapp-chatbot node dist/commands/news-cli.js 10

# Empty line required at end of cron file
